WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
Spring 2020. Shops shut their doors,

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.590
and people stayed at home.

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.040
In the UK, households saved
a record 29.1 per cent

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.850
of their income between April and June.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.230
In the US, the saving rate
hit 33 per cent in April.

6
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.290
Most incomes were protected.

7
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.760
Yet spending fell sharply.

8
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.690
So what makes a whole
country stop spending,

9
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.010
even when pay hasn't changed?

10
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.790
In this mission, you'll split
income into spending and saving,

11
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.430
and see what shifts aggregate demand.

12
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.330
Then you'll see how interest rates and
borrowing change what households spend.

13
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:42.270
Your mission: find out what really
drives a country's spending.
